# "If a player is dealt damage this way" is the player the damage reached (CR 120.3), not the target. Bot1's Show and Tell
# puts Screaming Nemesis onto the battlefield and Bot2 Ancient Adamantoise. Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills the Nemesis, whose
# trigger targets Bot2: the 3 damage is dealt to the Adamantoise instead (CR 614.1a), so Bot2 was dealt none, stays on 20 and
# can still gain life - Swords to Plowshares on its own Llanowar Elves gives it 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Screaming Nemesis
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ancient Adamantoise
Mountain
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Swords to Plowshares
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Screaming Nemesis)
Bot2.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Screaming Nemesis)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 3
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 21
Bot1.Graveyard = Screaming Nemesis; Show and Tell; Black Lotus
Exile = Llanowar Elves
